
## The icons

`src-tauri/icons/` holds the line's umbrella mark - lambda on graphite - until
the product has a mark of its own; `lyrn.toml` says `mark = "placeholder"`
meanwhile, and `assets/` holds the same mark as three master SVGs.

A mark of its own replaces those three masters, and `docs/export-assets.mjs`
draws every icon from them - it comes with the documentation site
(`lyrn new {{ name }} --form docs`). Not `pnpm tauri icon`: it cuts every size
from one picture, and the line's rule is that a size takes the level of the
mark that reads at it - S at 27px and under, M up to 63px, L above. In the
`.ico` the **largest image comes first**: Tauri takes the first entry for the
window, and a 16px one there leaves the title bar blurred.

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| `src/` | The interface |
| `src/components/ui/` | dowel's primitives, copied from the registry and held to it by `pnpm lint` |
| `src-tauri/src/lib.rs` | Where the application starts; `main.rs` is a thin shell |
| `src-tauri/src/commands.rs` | What the webview is allowed to call |
| `src-tauri/capabilities/` | The permissions the window is granted |
| `src-tauri/icons/` | The icons the bundle and the window use |
| `assets/` | The mark's three master SVGs |
| `tools/` | The registry and license checks `pnpm lint` and the audit run |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decisions, newest last |
